} "Cross Country Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "CUR"} "Curling"] "\n" [:option {:value "FSK"} "Figure Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "FRS"} "Freestyle Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "IHO"} "Ice Hockey"] "\n" [:option {:value "LUG"} "Luge"] "\n" [:option {:value "NCB"} "Nordic Combined"] "\n" [:option {:value "STK"} "Short Track Speed Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "SKN"} "Skeleton"] "\n" [:option {:value "SJP"} "Ski Jumping"] "\n" [:option {:value "SBD"} "Snowboarding"] "\n" [:option {:value "SSK"} "Speed Skating"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/57/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Bobsleigh in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "29"} "1924 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "30"} "1928 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "31"} "1932 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "32"} "1936 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "33"} "1948 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "34"} "1952 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "35"} "1956 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "37"} "1964 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "38"} "1968 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "39"} "1972 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "40"} "1976 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "41"} "1980 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "42"} "1984 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "43"} "1988 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "44"} "1992 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "45"} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "46"} "1998 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "47"} "2002 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "49"} "2006 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "66"} "2012 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "58"} "2014 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "68"} "2016 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "60"} "2018 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "70"} "2020 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "62"} "2022 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/BOB'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Bobsleigh at the 2010 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 27 February 2010"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "3"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/182"} "Whistler Sliding Centre, Whistler"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Situated on the slopes of Blackcomb Mountain the Whistler Sliding Centre hosted the bobsleigh, luge and skeleton events at the 2010 Winter Games.\nConstruction was completed in November 2007 and the following month the Canadian Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/91934"} "Pierre Lueders"] " had the honour of being the first man to pilot a bob down the course.\nFrom the outset the track gained a reputation as being both the fastest track in the world and one which demanded excellent technical ability.\nThe track was 1450 m in length with 16 corners with a vertical drop of 152 m and an average gradient of 10.5%. During the Games speeds regularly exceeded 145 km/h (90 mp/h) with " [:a {:href "/athletes/118682"} "Lyndon Rush"] "’s Canadian quartet posting the fastest speed at 153.4 km/h (95.3 mp/h)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Prior to the Games many nations complained about the amount of training that was allowed on the Olympic track.\nThe Canadian authorities only allowed foreign teams the minimum amount of runs permissible under Fédération Internationale de Bobsleigh et de Tobogganing (FIBT) regulations prior to the Games, a decision that some felt was against the Olympic spirit."] "\n\n" [:p {} "One innovation for 2010 was the presence of a third crew from some of the elite nations of the bobsleigh world. Prior to Vancouver a limit of two crews per nation has existed at all Winter Games."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With the death of the Georgian luger Nodar Kumaritashvili, there were many concerns over the safety of the track for the bobsleigh teams. There were a number of crashes during both practice and the events themselves although, fortunately, there were no serious injuries. Germany, a traditional power in this event, won one gold and two silver medals. " [:a {:href "/athletes/101869"} "André Lange"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/101871"} "Kevin Kuske"] " (GER) both added to their Olympic medal tally, adding gold and silver to the three gold medals won in previous Games. However Canada, on their home track, won three medals and the United States two, and in the process winning their first men’s bobsleigh gold medal since 1948. Russia were the only other medal winners, gaining a bronze in the two man event."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/924240"} "Two, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 21 February 2010"] "\n" [:td {} "56"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/924247"} "Four, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "26 – 27 February 2010"] "\n" [:td {} "101"] "\n" [:td {} "17"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/924254"} "Two, Women"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 – 24 February 2010"] "\n" [:td {} "42"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n15